  "evidencia": "Page: The Hand That Feeds. Sentence: It was also a crossover hit, crossing over to pop radio as their first top 40 radio hit since \"Closer\" and \"Hurt\" in 1994 and 1995, respectively, peaking at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart.\nPage: Closer (Nine Inch Nails song). Sentence: \"Closer\" is a song by American industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails from their second studio album, \"The Downward Spiral\" (1994).\nPage: Mark Romanek. Sentence: His most notable music videos include \"Hurt\" (Johnny Cash), \"Closer\" (Nine Inch Nails), \"Can't Stop\" (Red Hot Chili Peppers), \"Bedtime Story\" (Madonna), and \"Scream\" (Michael & Janet Jackson).\nPage: Can't Stop the Feeling!. Sentence: Directed by Mark Romanek, its music video was released on May 16, 2016, and follows Timberlake on a tour to everyday places as he dances through what a typical day might be—it was followed by a number of fan-made videos.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: The Hand That Feeds. Sentence: It was also a crossover hit, crossing over to pop radio as their first top 40 radio hit since \"Closer\" and \"Hurt\" in 1994 and 1995, respectively, peaking at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart.\nPage: Closer (Nine Inch Nails song). Sentence: \"Closer\" is a song by American industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails from their second studio album, \"The Downward Spiral\" (1994).\nPage: Mark Romanek. Sentence: His most notable music videos include \"Hurt\" (Johnny Cash), \"Closer\" (Nine Inch Nails), \"Can't Stop\" (Red Hot Chili Peppers), \"Bedtime Story\" (Madonna), and \"Scream\" (Michael & Janet Jackson).\nPage: Can't Stop the Feeling!. Sentence: Directed by Mark Romanek, its music video was released on May 16, 2016, and follows Timberlake on a tour to everyday places as he dances through what a typical day might be—it was followed by a number of fan-made videos.",
