        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8655f116-628a-59df-bc7d-e153dd941127",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"The Hand That Feeds\", \"Closer\", \"Hurt\", \"Can't Stop the Feeling!\"\n- People: Mark Romanek, Justin Timberlake, Johnny Cash, Madonna, Michael Jackson, Janet Jackson\n- Organizations: Nine Inch Nails, Red Hot Chili Peppers, Billboard\n- Concepts: music videos, pop radio, crossover hits, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- In 1994, Nine Inch Nails released \"Closer\" on their second studio album, \"The Downward Spiral\".\n- In 1994 and 1995, Nine Inch Nails had top 40 radio hits with \"Closer\" and \"Hurt\", respectively.\n- Mark Romanek directed notable music videos including Nine Inch Nails' \"Closer\", Johnny Cash's \"Hurt\", Red Hot Chili Peppers' \"Can't Stop\", Madonna's \"Bedtime Story\", and Michael and Janet Jackson's \"Scream\".\n- \"The Hand That Feeds\" became a crossover hit for Nine Inch Nails by crossing over to pop radio.\n- \"The Hand That Feeds\" was Nine Inch Nails' first top 40 radio hit since \"Closer\" and \"Hurt\" in 1994 and 1995.\n- \"The Hand That Feeds\" peaked at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart.\n- On May 16, 2016, the music video for Justin Timberlake's \"Can't Stop the Feeling!\" was released.\n- Mark Romanek directed the music video for Justin Timberlake's \"Can't Stop the Feeling!\".\n- The music video for \"Can't Stop the Feeling!\" shows Justin Timberlake dancing through everyday places during a typical day and was followed by many fan-made videos.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4dc25435-cb90-55fe-9cc8-ddf73439721b",
        "text": "Page: The Hand That Feeds. Sentence: It was also a crossover hit, crossing over to pop radio as their first top 40 radio hit since \"Closer\" and \"Hurt\" in 1994 and 1995, respectively, peaking at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart.\nPage: Closer (Nine Inch Nails song). Sentence: \"Closer\" is a song by American industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails from their second studio album, \"The Downward Spiral\" (1994).\nPage: Mark Romanek. Sentence: His most notable music videos include \"Hurt\" (Johnny Cash), \"Closer\" (Nine Inch Nails), \"Can't Stop\" (Red Hot Chili Peppers), \"Bedtime Story\" (Madonna), and \"Scream\" (Michael & Janet Jackson).\nPage: Can't Stop the Feeling!. Sentence: Directed by Mark Romanek, its music video was released on May 16, 2016, and follows Timberlake on a tour to everyday places as he dances through what a typical day might be—it was followed by a number of fan-made videos.",
